text:
laura: hitting a weird one in the new CLI helper used by sample-apps: when jsonMode=true and we pass enum schemas, the JS helper will coerce numbers to strings and validate as OK. Python SDK rejects.

laura: repro:
```js
// helper config in CLI sample
const helper = makeFnCallHelper({
  name: 'set_priority',
  arguments_schema: {
    type: 'object',
    properties: {
      priority: { type: 'string', enum: ['low','medium','high'] }
    },
    required: ['priority']
  },
  coerceTypes: true // default in CLI helper
})

// model returns 2 (number) in jsonMode
// helper coerces to '2' then accepts because enum check does string compare
```

sasha: whoa. coerceTypes was added to be forgiving for user input but i didn't expect it to run after jsonMode parsing. jsonMode should give us typed values from the model, not coerce them again.

kevin: that explains parity mismatch. Py helper does strict type validation and doesn't coerce by default. JS helper's post-parse coercion runs in the final validate step, letting numbers pass as strings.

jamie: this caused a production sample where priority=2 got accepted and later turned into an invalid downstream DB enum. we missed it in unit tests because tests used string outputs.

laura: short-term mitigation: set coerceTypes=false for function_call helpers when jsonMode=true in sample-app templates. i can open a patch.

kevin: long-term options: 1) change helper to run coercion before schema enum check only when input is raw text (not jsonMode), 2) introduce `strictEnums: true` that forces exact type+value matching, 3) add an integration test exercising numeric model outputs.

sasha: +1 for strictEnums default for function_call flows. Breaking change risk but safer. we can gate behind CLI opt-in for now and flip later. also add a lint warning when sample-app scaffolding sets coerceTypes with jsonMode.

devex-bot: Ticket created: DEVEX-1123 "fncall helper coercion accepts numeric enums in jsonMode" assigned to laura. https://tracker.internal/DEVEX-1123

laura: i'll do three things in the PR: tighten sample template to set coerceTypes=false when jsonMode, add strictEnums flag and opt-in in CLI, and add integration tests that assert model numeric outputs fail enum validation. will ping.

jamie: pls also add a short note in the SDK migration docs: "If you rely on enum types with jsonMode, disable coercion or enable strictEnums to avoid silent acceptance of wrong types."

kevin: i'll coordinate with release to include the lint warning in the next scaffold push.

sasha: thanks — moving to triage `devex:fncall-schema` and marking for SDK parity review.
